Given a sum element z and a right token of z, the right copy is the element of B whose carrier is the set of tokens of B whose right constructors lie in z. A finite subset W of that carrier is consistent because the right lift of W lies in z, so z makes the lift sum-consistent, the left projection of the lift is empty, and the resulting consistency of the right projection rewrites to consistency of W. The carrier is closed under entailment from W. If W is empty, entailment transitivity through the given right token produces an entailment from that singleton, which is a sum entailment of the right constructor, and closure of z applies. If W is nonempty, the same closure applies to the right lift of W, whose right projection equals W.
